{
  "_comment": [
    "SimpleJellyMus - how the raw genre tags are turned into canonical styles.",
    "",
    "This is a behaviour file, not a vocabulary file: the vocabulary (which styles",
    "exist, and their spelling variants) lives in data/styles.json. Edit this one",
    "when a tag needs interpreting rather than translating.",
    "",
    "  drop           whole tag means nothing at all (websites, ripper junk)",
    "  drop_parts     pieces inside a compound tag to ignore (modifiers, formats)",
    "  strip_words    words removed from a piece before it is looked up",
    "  strip_regex    regular expressions removed from a tag before it is split",
    "  replace        normalised piece -> normalised piece (typos, ambiguous tags)",
    "  force          whole normalised tag -> list of style names (no splitting)",
    "  family_only    tags that only state a family, never a style",
    "  family_keywords  last resort: a piece containing this word is filed under",
    "                   that family with a low confidence (never invented as a style)",
    "",
    "After editing run:  python3 step3_vocabulary.py --all && python3 step4_normalize.py"
  ],
